A||||3||the need for speed||windshield wipers drain my battery ?????||||1||
Z||000000||the need for speed||11-28-2001||06:44 PM||||when it rains and I have to use the windshield wipers, the battery will slowly drain on the gauge and the lights will go low and the wipers will slow down. then after a little bit I will here a loud squeal and then the battery gauge will jump back up,and every thing runs good for a little wile then is dose it again??? any help I need it ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Phil||11-28-2001||06:48 PM||||Your alt. belt is either worn or loose- replace or tighten. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||the need for speed||11-29-2001||11:44 AM||||it is a new belt. i have adjusted it so it does not squeal any more it was doing it every morning but not any more,just when i use my window wipers||||reg||1
Z||000003||Pyric||11-29-2001||06:35 PM||||Check all of the connections and pieces after the switch,  the wiper circuit only consists on the Switch, motor and fuse.  Sound like something in that circuit is draining your battery faster than the alternator can recharge it.  <P>Try checking the voltage to ground with a volt meter from the plug into the wiper motor. (with the ignition on, but no engine running)<P>in an 85 GT the wires are colored WHT, GRY and PPL.<P>The WHT always has power on it, the GRY has power when wiper switch is on and in MIST, PULSE, LO or HIGH, and the PPL has power only in HIGH.<P>The resistance between the WHT and GRY should be between 500K ohms and 10k ohms.<P>Hope that helps  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ||||reg||1
